+#### Testing with State
+
+The harness supports stateful PTFs. State parameters (scalar state, `ListView`, `MapView`, and POJO/structured types)
+are no longer rejected. State is keyed by the partition key, and you can set the initial state for a given key
+via `.withInitialStateForKey(stateName, partitionKey, state)`.
+
+{{< tabs "state" >}}
+{{< tab "Java" >}}
+```java
+public class CountPTF extends ProcessTableFunction<Row> {
+  public void eval(
+      @ArgumentHint({ArgumentTrait.SET_SEMANTIC_TABLE, ArgumentTrait.OPTIONAL_PARTITION_BY})
+          Row input,
+      @StateHint DataTypeHint("BIGINT") long count) {
+    count++;
+    collect(Row.of(count));
+  }
+}
+
+@Test
+void testStateful() throws Exception {
+  try (ProcessTableFunctionTestHarness<Row> harness =
+    ProcessTableFunctionTestHarness.ofClass(CountPTF.class)
+    .withTableArgument("input", DataTypes.of("ROW<value INT>"))
+    .withInitialStateForKey("count", Row.of(42), 10L)
+    .build()) {
+
+    harness.processElement(Row.of(1));
+    assertThat(harness.getOutput()).containsExactly(Row.of(11L));
+  }
+}
+```
+{{< /tab >}}
+{{< /tabs >}}
+
+**Note**: State TTL is not supported by the test harness.
+
